From 6de2ab48c938a53d44e6a6989a1750991a557807 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phase14 audit <audit@local>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 05:41:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/20] fix(redirects): retarget legacy LEGIC / MIFARE-sticker
 / reader rules, collapse chains, review homepage catch-alls
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 14 batch B4 (audit 2026-09-01, Phase 2 T5 / Phase 7 §7). 38 rules
changed in vercel.json, mirrored in public/_redirects and
ROUTE_CANONICAL_OVERRIDES (legacy HTML canonicals). No sources added or
removed; every new destination is an existing 200 page in the build.
- /product/legic-card/ -> /products/rfid-cards/legic-card/ (DE/ES legacy
  rules already pointed at the product page)
- /product/mifare-stickers/ -> /products/rfid-labels/ (chip mismatch with the
  NTAG213 SKU; ES/RU legacy rules already use the category)
- nfc-reader-writer-with-free-sdks in ja/tr/it/fr/es/da -> the desktop NFC
  reader/encoder page, matching the EN rule
- 3 two-hop chains via typo destinations collapsed to direct rules
- 25 of the 43 '-> /' rules retargeted: language blog indexes -> /blog/,
  shop indexes -> /products/all/, TR FAQ -> /faq/, ZH contact -> /contact/,
  legacy product URLs (ru/ja/it/fr/he/fa) -> the product family or the
  exact product page; the 13 language homes and cart/checkout/my-account
  catch-alls keep '/'
- FeliCa / HITAG rules unchanged (product status is an owner decision)
See AUDIT_2026-09-01/phase14/B4-redirect-changes.csv for every rule.
